  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> capacitors, each of capacitance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are connected in&nbsp;parallel and are&nbsp;charged by a source of potential difference <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> capacitors, each of capacitance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are connected in series and are charged by&nbsp;a source of potential difference <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>V</mi></math>.&nbsp;If both the combinations have the same total energy, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. What is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A parallel combination of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math>capacitors each of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/abs/8146f98e-17d5-4a6c-b380-d7c228bbb11f-2.PNG\" style=\"width: 199px; height: 172px;\" /></p><p>Total energy stored in parallel combination,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>A series combination of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> capacitors each of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>are connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> source.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/abs/0e0cb667-5992-4155-83e6-efa7237e80f0-3.PNG\" style=\"width: 204px; height: 127px;\" /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Total energy stored in series combination,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>16</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>According to give<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>n probelm,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></math></p><p>From equations,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
